# Register a new object in the world (perception saw something new).
# held_by is deliberately absent: "which gripper holds this object" is robot
# proprioception owned by the backend (set_held_by), not something perception
# observes. A newly added object is registered as held by nobody.
# Refused (success=false) for an object_id already in the scene, a blank
# label/object_id, or a pose the store rejects.
string object_id
string label
geometry_msgs/Pose pose
bool graspable
---
# success=true means the write committed atomically to disk; error is empty.
# success=false means the write did NOT durably commit. Two cases, told apart
# by error: the store refused the input and left the scene unchanged, or the
# atomic disk write failed and the change is held in the store's memory to be
# re-written on the next mutation (robot_world's dirty-flag design, D23) --
# not "rejected".
bool success
string error
